  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile this fix prevents the `AttributeError` during module import, it is incomplete because the registration logic for these patterns (around line 306) is not guarded by the same check. On CUDA platforms where the custom op is missing, `ActivationQuantFusionPass` will still attempt to register `SiluMulBlockQuantPattern`, which will trigger an `AssertionError` at line 73 because the keys will be missing from `FUSED_OPS`.\n\nTo fix this properly and maintain consistency with other fused ops (like `nvfp4` at line 42), you should define a support flag here and use it to guard the registration loop as well.\n\n```suggestion\nsilu_and_mul_per_block_quant_supported = (\n    current_platform.is_cuda_alike()\n    and hasattr(torch.ops._C, \"silu_and_mul_per_block_quant\"))\n\nif silu_and_mul_per_block_quant_supported:\n    FUSED_OPS[kFp8Dynamic128Sym] = torch.ops._C.silu_and_mul_per_block_quant.default\n    FUSED_OPS[kFp8Dynamic64Sym] = torch.ops._C.silu_and_mul_per_block_quant.default\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-04-15T03:32:52Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -45,7 +45,9 @@\n if silu_and_mul_nvfp4_quant_supported:\n     FUSED_OPS[kNvfp4Dynamic] = torch.ops._C.silu_and_mul_nvfp4_quant.default  # noqa: E501\n \n-if current_platform.is_cuda_alike():\n+if current_platform.is_cuda_alike() and hasattr(\n+    torch.ops._C, \"silu_and_mul_per_block_quant\"\n+):\n     FUSED_OPS[kFp8Dynamic128Sym] = torch.ops._C.silu_and_mul_per_block_quant.default\n     FUSED_OPS[kFp8Dynamic64Sym] = torch.ops._C.silu_and_mul_per_block_quant.default",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/39865#discussion_r3083788643",
      "id": 3083788643,
